WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.292
- Good morning Believe Nation,

00:00:01.292 --> 00:00:04.380
my name is Evan Carmichael,
my one word is believe,

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.802
and I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:05.802 --> 00:00:09.332
are going to solve all of
the world's major problems.

00:00:09.332 --> 00:00:10.655
So to help you on your journey today

00:00:10.655 --> 00:00:14.742
we're going to learn how
to build a great team.

00:00:14.742 --> 00:00:16.592
Over to you Kandi Burruss.

00:00:16.592 --> 00:00:18.879
(shouting rooster)

00:00:18.879 --> 00:00:21.400
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.264
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:24.264 --> 00:00:28.089
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:28.089 --> 00:00:30.241
- It's always good is
if you can get somebody

00:00:30.241 --> 00:00:34.261
to partner up with you
and with other businesses.

00:00:34.261 --> 00:00:36.923
Because for me, I have a business partner

00:00:36.923 --> 00:00:38.693
with tags in my stores, I have a business

00:00:38.693 --> 00:00:41.137
partner with Bedroom Kandi.

00:00:41.137 --> 00:00:44.138
If it wasn't for that, I wouldn't be able

00:00:44.138 --> 00:00:45.698
to do all the things that I'm doin'.

00:00:45.698 --> 00:00:48.762
But because I do have
great business partners,

00:00:48.762 --> 00:00:51.938
they help me keep those things going.

00:00:51.938 --> 00:00:54.231
So you have to have a great team.

00:00:54.231 --> 00:00:56.081
You by yourself, it
probably wouldn't work.

00:00:56.081 --> 00:00:58.920
You can't be but in so
many places at one time,

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.988
so you have to have
people to see your vision

00:01:01.988 --> 00:01:04.329
and help make your vision happen.

00:01:04.329 --> 00:01:06.069
- You can't do everything yourself

00:01:06.069 --> 00:01:07.846
if you want to be a
successful entrepreneur.

00:01:07.846 --> 00:01:09.750
There are only so many hours in a day

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.781
and you only have so much limited ability,

00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:14.719
that if you try to do everything

00:01:14.719 --> 00:01:16.953
in your business and never look to scale

00:01:16.953 --> 00:01:19.015
or grow, then you're going to be limited

00:01:19.015 --> 00:01:21.270
in how much you can do and
how much you can accomplish.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.891
Now at the start, you
do everything yourself.

00:01:23.891 --> 00:01:27.654
At the start, you boost up,
you hustle, you find ways.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.489
But quickly, you need to figure out what

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:33.649
is a thing that you are
among the best people

00:01:33.649 --> 00:01:37.500
in the world at or have
that world-class potential?

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.737
You are genius-level talent at something.

00:01:40.737 --> 00:01:41.959
What is that?

00:01:41.959 --> 00:01:43.834
Figure that out and spend as much time

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:46.615
in that lane as possible, and then look

00:01:46.615 --> 00:01:49.451
to expand by building up people who

00:01:49.451 --> 00:01:51.248
are great at all the
things you're not good at.

00:01:51.248 --> 00:01:52.088
Here are a couple of the pitfalls

00:01:52.088 --> 00:01:54.579
that people falter when they
go through this process.

00:01:54.579 --> 00:01:56.451
First off, rarely the first person

00:01:56.451 --> 00:01:58.884
that you hire is a good fit.

00:01:58.884 --> 00:02:00.953
They may have the skills that you want,

00:02:00.953 --> 00:02:02.916
but your values don't align, right?

00:02:02.916 --> 00:02:04.249
You don't have similar one words,

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:05.914
you haven't gone through that process,

00:02:05.914 --> 00:02:08.035
your values don't align
and so it falls apart.

00:02:08.035 --> 00:02:10.502
You also likely suck as a leader.

00:02:10.502 --> 00:02:13.690
Part of now building a team
is you need to lead a team.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:14.702
You need to be a good manager,

00:02:14.702 --> 00:02:16.165
you have to care about your people

00:02:16.165 --> 00:02:18.049
and not just about them
getting the work done,

00:02:18.049 --> 00:02:19.296
but care about them as human beings

00:02:19.296 --> 00:02:20.138
and what they're going through

00:02:20.138 --> 00:02:22.288
and how you can help, and how
you can be supportive to them.

00:02:22.288 --> 00:02:25.725
So a lot of times, that
first hire doesn't work out.

00:02:25.725 --> 00:02:28.799
And here's what happens
to so many entrepreneurs.

00:02:28.799 --> 00:02:31.239
That person didn't work out, I can't build

00:02:31.239 --> 00:02:33.347
a team, that was a stupid idea,

00:02:33.347 --> 00:02:35.558
I'm just going to go back
to doing everything myself

00:02:35.558 --> 00:02:37.904
because it was so much easier.

00:02:37.904 --> 00:02:40.401
And then you end up playing small again.

00:02:40.401 --> 00:02:41.932
So what ends up happening when you hire

00:02:41.932 --> 00:02:44.913
is they take up a lot of your time,

00:02:44.913 --> 00:02:46.739
there's a learning
curve, they may have some

00:02:46.739 --> 00:02:48.003
problems at the beginning.

00:02:48.003 --> 00:02:50.108
But by working through
that and maybe getting rid

00:02:50.108 --> 00:02:51.899
of them and bringing somebody else in,

00:02:51.899 --> 00:02:53.692
work it through that
getting the right people

00:02:53.692 --> 00:02:55.346
in place, that's when you can go

00:02:55.346 --> 00:02:58.603
and explode and do much
more meaningful work,

00:02:58.603 --> 00:03:00.124
spend your time doing the things

00:03:00.124 --> 00:03:01.878
that make you a lot more excited,

00:03:01.878 --> 00:03:03.509
and have a much bigger impact.

00:03:03.509 --> 00:03:04.818
A lot of people also
say, well I don't have

00:03:04.818 --> 00:03:06.199
the money to go out and hire somebody,

00:03:06.199 --> 00:03:08.308
I can't afford to go
out and hire somebody.

00:03:08.308 --> 00:03:09.708
How am I going to build a team?

00:03:09.708 --> 00:03:11.543
I can't even pay myself.

00:03:11.543 --> 00:03:13.114
Well, a couple ideas.

00:03:13.114 --> 00:03:14.266
One, you don't necessarily need

00:03:14.266 --> 00:03:16.184
to hire somebody right now.

00:03:16.184 --> 00:03:17.586
As long as it's on your roadmap,

00:03:17.586 --> 00:03:19.087
as long as it's something
that you're constantly

00:03:19.087 --> 00:03:21.635
paying attention to that is in your vision

00:03:21.635 --> 00:03:23.436
so that you are not going
to be doing this alone

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.766
for the rest of your life.

00:03:24.766 --> 00:03:26.434
Two, you can look at hiring somebody

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:27.757
on a part-time basis.

00:03:27.757 --> 00:03:30.458
The first person I hired
was for one hour a day,

00:03:30.458 --> 00:03:32.116
one hour a day doing database work

00:03:32.116 --> 00:03:34.055
for me because he was
better at it than I was

00:03:34.055 --> 00:03:35.695
and he freed up an hour and a half

00:03:35.695 --> 00:03:38.766
of my time to go off and do other things

00:03:38.766 --> 00:03:40.689
that I enjoyed more and I was better at

00:03:40.689 --> 00:03:42.475
and could help build the business.

00:03:42.475 --> 00:03:44.628
So you could hire somebody for an hour

00:03:44.628 --> 00:03:46.336
a day or a couple of hours a week just

00:03:46.336 --> 00:03:49.369
to free up some of that work
that you don't want to do

00:03:49.369 --> 00:03:51.224
to focus on bigger things.

00:03:51.224 --> 00:03:53.215
And three, you can also look for people

00:03:53.215 --> 00:03:54.747
to volunteer or to be a part.

00:03:54.747 --> 00:03:56.388
It might be a partnership in your business

00:03:56.388 --> 00:03:58.596
and you're both putting sweat equity in.

00:03:58.596 --> 00:04:00.366
It might be mentoring somebody who

00:04:00.366 --> 00:04:02.967
is a high school intern
or a university intern

00:04:02.967 --> 00:04:04.607
and bringing them into your business.

00:04:04.607 --> 00:04:06.725
Now you have to do your job
of actually mentoring them,

00:04:06.725 --> 00:04:08.812
but they're looking
more for the experience

00:04:08.812 --> 00:04:11.021
of being involved in
what you're doing than

00:04:11.021 --> 00:04:13.577
for monetary compensation, right?

00:04:13.577 --> 00:04:16.167
They're getting a grade at their school,

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:17.806
so they have to do a good job and that's

00:04:17.806 --> 00:04:18.993
what they're looking for, much more

00:04:18.993 --> 00:04:20.076
than getting paid to do it.

00:04:20.076 --> 00:04:21.784
So there's always other options,

00:04:21.784 --> 00:04:22.842
and one of the most important things

00:04:22.842 --> 00:04:24.613
that you need to understand
as an entrepreneur

00:04:24.613 --> 00:04:26.122
is you need to be resourceful.

00:04:26.122 --> 00:04:29.022
You will get these kinds
of problems, constantly.

00:04:29.022 --> 00:04:30.943
I need to bring on a
team, but I can't afford

00:04:30.943 --> 00:04:32.882
to do it, how do I do that?

00:04:32.882 --> 00:04:34.611
I need to go and market my company,

00:04:34.611 --> 00:04:37.308
but I can't afford to take
out an ad on the Super Bowl,

00:04:37.308 --> 00:04:38.876
so how do I go and do that, right?

00:04:38.876 --> 00:04:41.277
You will constantly
have these restrictions

00:04:41.277 --> 00:04:43.345
and restraints that are put on you

00:04:43.345 --> 00:04:44.681
as you try to build the business.

00:04:44.681 --> 00:04:46.663
You are constantly lacking in resources

00:04:46.663 --> 00:04:50.088
and so, you succeed by being resourceful,

00:04:50.088 --> 00:04:52.863
by finding another way, by being creative,

00:04:52.863 --> 00:04:54.788
by understanding people and what they need

00:04:54.788 --> 00:04:56.187
and how you might be
able to give it to them

00:04:56.187 --> 00:04:57.602
in a non-monetary way.

00:04:57.602 --> 00:04:59.498
That's the game of entrepreneurship.

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:02.636
I was able to greatly
expand my businesses,

00:05:02.636 --> 00:05:04.100
my YouTube channel, since that's

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:05.972
what you may be more familiar with.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:07.556
At the beginning it was me doing videos

00:05:07.556 --> 00:05:10.806
all by myself, and I would make a video

00:05:13.045 --> 00:05:16.616
at most once a week,
but usually maybe once

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:18.758
a month or twice a month.

00:05:18.758 --> 00:05:21.478
And then as I brought my
first editor on-board,

00:05:21.478 --> 00:05:22.749
that's when I was able to go from once

00:05:22.749 --> 00:05:25.211
a week max to once a day.

00:05:25.211 --> 00:05:26.833
That was a huge increase right?

00:05:26.833 --> 00:05:28.500
Seven times or more.

00:05:29.525 --> 00:05:30.798
And then when I got a second editor,

00:05:30.798 --> 00:05:32.636
when I got researchers I can move up,

00:05:32.636 --> 00:05:34.697
and I went to two a day
and went to three a day.

00:05:34.697 --> 00:05:37.933
And so you can greatly
improve your productivity

00:05:37.933 --> 00:05:39.482
by building the team and I get to focus

00:05:39.482 --> 00:05:40.404
on what I love doing.

00:05:40.404 --> 00:05:42.112
I don't like editing.

00:05:42.112 --> 00:05:44.329
That's not what I love,
Christina loves editing.

00:05:44.329 --> 00:05:45.662
Christina's editing this video,

00:05:45.662 --> 00:05:47.086
you know I love you Christina.

00:05:47.086 --> 00:05:48.526
Christina loves editing,
it's what she loves

00:05:48.526 --> 00:05:49.667
to do and what she's great at.

00:05:49.667 --> 00:05:50.750
It's amazing.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.613
I love being in front of the camera

00:05:52.613 --> 00:05:55.379
and it's the highest value
that I can bring to the team.

00:05:55.379 --> 00:05:56.989
If it relied on me being a great editor,

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:58.789
this company would fail.

00:05:58.789 --> 00:06:00.420
'Cause it's not something
that I actually want

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.797
to learn to get better at.

00:06:01.797 --> 00:06:04.388
There's this old saying,
if you want to go far,

00:06:04.388 --> 00:06:05.836
you go with the team.

00:06:05.836 --> 00:06:07.925
If you want to go fast, you go alone.

00:06:07.925 --> 00:06:09.813
And so stop focusing
on the short-term game

00:06:09.813 --> 00:06:13.342
of just going fast, think
long-term, think bigger-picture,

00:06:13.342 --> 00:06:14.958
think going far, think about the vision,

00:06:14.958 --> 00:06:16.738
think about what you're
trying to accomplish.

00:06:16.738 --> 00:06:18.659
You need a team to help you get there.

00:06:18.659 --> 00:06:20.132
So the question then today is,

00:06:20.132 --> 00:06:22.197
I'm curious, who was the first person

00:06:22.197 --> 00:06:25.457
that you hired on your
team that added incremental

00:06:25.457 --> 00:06:27.613
improvement and you
saw big business growth

00:06:27.613 --> 00:06:29.634
because of it, or if
you haven't hired yet,

00:06:29.634 --> 00:06:31.979
who is the first person that you need

00:06:31.979 --> 00:06:35.258
on your team to be able to blast through?

00:06:35.258 --> 00:06:36.488
Really curious to find out, leave

00:06:36.488 --> 00:06:37.812
it down in the comments below.

00:06:37.812 --> 00:06:38.813
I also want to give a quick shout-out

00:06:38.813 --> 00:06:43.458
to coach Bailey Cooper from
canvassingcoachaustintx.com.

00:06:43.458 --> 00:06:44.479
Thank you so much for picking up

00:06:44.479 --> 00:06:46.465
a copy of my book, Your One Word.

00:06:46.465 --> 00:06:48.389
I really, really, really
appreciate the support

00:06:48.389 --> 00:06:49.821
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:06:49.821 --> 00:06:51.370
So thank you guys again for watching,

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:52.387
I believe in you.

00:06:52.387 --> 00:06:54.499
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:06:54.499 --> 00:06:56.838
and whatever your one word is.

00:06:56.838 --> 00:06:59.050
Much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:02.040
for another shot of espresso.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.825
♫ I wake up every morning

00:07:04.825 --> 00:07:08.242
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:07:10.708 --> 00:07:12.129
- Over the next five years, we plan

00:07:12.129 --> 00:07:15.553
to take on the banking community,

00:07:15.553 --> 00:07:17.382
we plan to take on the cosmetics industry,

00:07:17.382 --> 00:07:19.940
we plan to take on the clothing industry

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:22.961
and telecommunications, and
one or two other industries

00:07:22.961 --> 00:07:24.493
and see whether we can give them

00:07:24.493 --> 00:07:27.165
a run for their money and
do it slightly differently

00:07:27.165 --> 00:07:28.312
than it's been done before.

00:07:28.312 --> 00:07:31.062
- Why do you think you can do it?

00:07:32.112 --> 00:07:33.210
- Mainly because I think we've got

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.859
a fantastic team of people.

00:07:35.859 --> 00:07:37.461
We attract good people.

00:07:37.461 --> 00:07:39.301
- And their skills are translatable

00:07:39.301 --> 00:07:41.281
to whatever the industry is.

00:07:41.281 --> 00:07:45.266
It's creativity, it's risk
orientation, it's what?

00:07:45.266 --> 00:07:47.629
- I think if you can
run one business well,

00:07:47.629 --> 00:07:49.439
you can run any business.

00:07:49.439 --> 00:07:51.410
And if you know that what matters

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:53.891
in business is a good team of people,

00:07:53.891 --> 00:07:58.556
well-motivated team of
people, incentivized well,

00:07:58.556 --> 00:07:59.689
given a lot of freedom to go out

00:07:59.689 --> 00:08:03.889
and prove themselves, you can
pretty well achieve anything.

00:08:03.889 --> 00:08:08.056
- [Interviewer] What do you
credit for your success?

00:08:09.124 --> 00:08:11.775
- I mean you got to have a great team.

00:08:11.775 --> 00:08:13.620
It's all about having the
right people around you.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:17.050
- Surprised, surprised by
the night of turn-up, whoa.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:20.274
♫ Whoa, it's just me, myself, and I.

00:08:20.274 --> 00:08:24.441
- Both for solid workers, but
also just positive influences

00:08:25.353 --> 00:08:26.617
to you, you know what I mean?

00:08:26.617 --> 00:08:28.041
People that inspire you, people who bring

00:08:28.041 --> 00:08:30.505
good energy every day.

00:08:30.505 --> 00:08:34.195
That and just hardworking dedication.

00:08:34.195 --> 00:08:37.070
- You sound so passionate
about so many diverse pieces

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:40.328
of your life that the big question is,

00:08:40.328 --> 00:08:41.767
how do you juggle all that?

00:08:41.767 --> 00:08:44.764
How do you make all of that
happen and successfully

00:08:44.764 --> 00:08:47.342
from your music career to being a mom,

00:08:47.342 --> 00:08:49.469
to being a life partner, all of that

00:08:49.469 --> 00:08:52.802
is so hard to juggle, how do you do it?

00:08:52.802 --> 00:08:55.570
What's the secret behind that?

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:58.197
- I don't know how I'm
going to keep doin' it.

00:08:58.197 --> 00:09:00.511
That's a good question.

00:09:00.511 --> 00:09:03.422
'Cause with a baby, things
tend to change a lot,

00:09:03.422 --> 00:09:06.760
but I have a great team,
people who understand me

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:09.646
very well who understand my cause,

00:09:09.646 --> 00:09:12.479
my commitment, and who support him

00:09:13.878 --> 00:09:15.822
and make my life easier.

00:09:15.822 --> 00:09:18.018
So it is very important
to be well-surrounded.

